# Commit messages

Every commit subject starts with the Jira ticket key for the work, so the key is the first thing visible in `git log`.

## Format

```
TICKET-KEY: Short imperative summary
```

- The key is the project prefix plus the number, as in `BUILDSYS-640`.
- One space after the colon. The rest of the subject stays a short imperative sentence.
- The body may explain why. It does not replace the key on the subject line.
- Use the same key on every commit for that ticket, including follow-up fixes on the same branch.

## Examples

```
BUILDSYS-640: Emit I* aliases for simple ASN.1 typedefs.

BUILDSYS-645: Add optional per-invoke timeout on the ROSE wire.
```

## When the key is unknown

Ask for the ticket key before committing. Do not invent a key, and do not commit with the key only in the body or at the end of the subject.